---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import FlowDiagram from "../components/FlowDiagram.astro";
import ExperienceJourney from "../components/ExperienceJourney.astro";
---
<Layout title="Ken Lim — Data & AI, end to end" description="Ken Lim builds the full data stack end to end — ingesting raw data, delivering high-quality governed tables and trained, tuned models, to shipped data and AI products. 18+ years across fintech, healthtech, proptech and the public sector.">

  <!-- letterhead / hero -->
  <section class="pt-14 pb-12 text-center sm:pt-20">
    <p class="font-mono text-[11px] uppercase tracking-[0.35em] text-amber-700 dark:text-amber-400">Data &amp; AI · End to End</p>
    <h1 class="mt-4 text-5xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-6xl">Ken Lim</h1>
    <p class="mx-auto mt-5 max-w-xl text-lg leading-relaxed text-stone-600 dark:text-stone-300">
      I build the <span class="text-stone-900 dark:text-stone-100">full data stack</span> — from ingesting raw data,
      through high-quality, governed tables and trained, tuned models, to shipped data &amp; AI products.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-4 font-mono text-[11px] uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-stone-400 dark:text-stone-500">
      18+ years · fintech · healthtech · proptech · public sector · U.S. citizen
    </p>
    <div class="mt-6 flex flex-wrap justify-center gap-x-6 gap-y-2 font-mono text-[12px]">
      <a class="text-amber-700 hover:underline dark:text-amber-400" href="mailto:mail@kennylim.com">mail@kennylim.com</a>
      <a class="text-stone-500 hover:text-stone-900 dark:text-stone-400 dark:hover:text-stone-100" href="tel:+19298889061">+1 (929) 888-9061</a>
      <a class="text-stone-500 hover:text-stone-900 dark:text-stone-400 dark:hover:text-stone-100" href="https://linkedin.com/in/kenny-lim" rel="noopener" target="_blank">LinkedIn ↗</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 1. about me -->
  <section class="border-t border-stone-200/80 py-12 dark:border-stone-800">
    <h2 class="font-mono text-[11px] uppercase tracking-[0.3em] text-stone-400 dark:text-stone-500">About me</h2>
    <div class="mt-5 space-y-4 text-[16px] leading-relaxed text-stone-600 dark:text-stone-300">
      <p>
        Most AI initiatives don't fail at the model — they fail at the data. So I work end to
        end across the full data stack: ingesting raw data, pipelines and transformation,
        governed data platforms, the ML platforms they feed, and the AI services — agents, RAG,
        MCP — running in production. I've built and scaled every one of those layers myself, so
        there are no gaps or handoff losses between them.
      </p>
      <p>
        I'm a hands-on data tech lead. I set strategy, design the architecture, write
        production code, and build the people around me — mentoring and coaching in-house
        teams and leading onshore and offshore contractors. Some of the work takes elbow
        grease: the tenacity and grit to sit with complex, messy data until it becomes clean,
        governed tables. And because I run and maintain my own production platforms day to
        day, there's no gap between the decision and the consequence — I have the full picture
        and a feedback loop that closes on its own.
      </p>
      <p>
        For 18+ years that has spanned fintech, healthtech, consumer and enterprise SaaS,
        proptech and the public sector — twice through acquisition. A decade of consulting
        first, delivering big-data builds on a modern stack across finance, government, health,
        retail and utilities worldwide, shaped how I work: pragmatic, results-driven,
        cost-conscious and transparent.
        It also taught me the most useful lesson of the job — the right architecture is the one
        the client can run after the consultant leaves.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 2. what I do -->
  <section id="do" class="scroll-mt-6 border-t border-stone-200/80 py-12 dark:border-stone-800">
    <h2 class="font-mono text-[11px] uppercase tracking-[0.3em] text-stone-400 dark:text-stone-500">What I do</h2>
    <div class="mt-5 space-y-4 text-[16px] leading-relaxed text-stone-600 dark:text-stone-300">
      <p>
        The five stages below are what I deliver on every engagement — what each one produces,
        and the production practices that run through all of them.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="mt-9">
      <FlowDiagram />
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 3. experience, long form -->
  <section id="experience" data-tabgroup class="scroll-mt-6 border-t border-stone-200/80 py-12 dark:border-stone-800">
    <div class="flex items-center justify-between gap-4">
      <h2 class="font-mono text-[11px] uppercase tracking-[0.3em] text-stone-400 dark:text-stone-500">My experience</h2>
      <div class="flex gap-1 font-mono text-[10px] uppercase tracking-wider" role="tablist">
        <button data-view="line" class="tab-btn rounded px-2.5 py-1 transition-colors">Timeline</button>
        <button data-view="prose" class="tab-btn rounded px-2.5 py-1 transition-colors">Full text</button>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div data-view="line" class="tab-panel mt-6">
      <ExperienceJourney />
    </div>
    <div data-view="prose" class="tab-panel hidden">
    <p class="mt-5 max-w-2xl text-[16px] leading-relaxed text-stone-600 dark:text-stone-300">
      Hands-on data engineering leader with 18+ years architecting, developing, scaling and
      maintaining production data and AI platforms across fintech, healthtech, real estate and
      the public sector — U.S. banking compliance systems, AI-driven therapy, and now nuclear
      safeguards. The common thread: being accountable end to end, from the whiteboard to the
      on-call rotation, and leaving teams and platforms stronger than the projects that needed them.
    </p>
    <div class="mt-8 space-y-8">
      <div>
        <h3 class="text-[17px] font-semibold text-stone-900 dark:text-stone-100">International Atomic Energy Agency <span class="font-normal text-stone-400 dark:text-stone-500">— Senior Data Engineer / Architect · 2024–present</span></h3>
        <ul class="mt-2 list-disc space-y-1.5 pl-5 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-stone-600 dark:text-stone-300">
          <li>Architect and hands-on engineer of SG Lake — a greenfield, open-source, air-gapped lakehouse on Kubernetes consolidating Safeguards data for analytics and AI.</li>
          <li>Authored the platform architecture and white paper, audited by PwC against all five Well-Architected pillars.</li>
          <li>Production ingestion services, Airflow pipelines and dbt models on Apache Iceberg; Trino for federated query, Spark for transformation; deploying, scaling and maintaining it as multiple project teams onboard.</li>
          <li>Built the observability and quality stack — Prometheus/Grafana SLOs, data contracts, dbt tests, Great Expectations, OpenMetadata lineage. The gold layer is the single source of truth for the agency's data science and AI teams.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h3 class="text-[17px] font-semibold text-stone-900 dark:text-stone-100">Reach Financial <span class="font-normal text-stone-400 dark:text-stone-500">— Lead Data Engineer · NYC · 2023–2024</span></h3>
        <ul class="mt-2 list-disc space-y-1.5 pl-5 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-stone-600 dark:text-stone-300">
          <li>Technical lead owning data strategy and roadmap while writing production code.</li>
          <li>Delivered AI products for credit scoring, loan origination and risk — contract-tested feature tables for the ML team on Snowflake, dbt and Dagster, with a domain-driven Data Mesh.</li>
          <li>Resolved a persistent Salesforce→Snowflake dynamic-pricing sync failure that had outlived multiple attempts.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h3 class="text-[17px] font-semibold text-stone-900 dark:text-stone-100">Kaia Health <span class="font-normal text-stone-400 dark:text-stone-500">— Lead Data Engineer · NYC · 2021–2023 · acquired by Sword Health</span></h3>
        <ul class="mt-2 list-disc space-y-1.5 pl-5 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-stone-600 dark:text-stone-300">
          <li>Architected, developed and operated the production Snowflake platform behind AI-driven musculoskeletal therapy.</li>
          <li>Led the Redshift→Snowflake migration end to end, designing Medallion and Lambda architectures for AI model training; Airflow and dbt pipelines feeding proprietary algorithms, with Great Expectations checks guarding production ML models.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h3 class="text-[17px] font-semibold text-stone-900 dark:text-stone-100">Thinx <span class="font-normal text-stone-400 dark:text-stone-500">— Lead Data Engineer · NYC · 2021 · acquired by Kimberly-Clark</span></h3>
        <ul class="mt-2 list-disc space-y-1.5 pl-5 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-stone-600 dark:text-stone-300">
          <li>Architected and developed the data platform from scratch — Airflow, AWS S3, Snowflake — integrating vendor systems (NetSuite, Tatari, Loop, Friendbuy, FormKeep), with reusable pipeline patterns, containerized deployments and CI/CD.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h3 class="text-[17px] font-semibold text-stone-900 dark:text-stone-100">N26 <span class="font-normal text-stone-400 dark:text-stone-500">— Senior Data Engineer · NYC/Berlin · 2019–2021</span></h3>
        <ul class="mt-2 list-disc space-y-1.5 pl-5 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-stone-600 dark:text-stone-300">
          <li>Architected, developed and administered the production U.S. data platform (PostgreSQL, custom pipelines, Metabase) as part of the core global data team.</li>
          <li>Partnered with Compliance on fraud-risk audits, mitigation systems and regulatory workflows for the U.S. banking entity.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h3 class="text-[17px] font-semibold text-stone-900 dark:text-stone-100">Cherre <span class="font-normal text-stone-400 dark:text-stone-500">— Senior Data Engineer · NYC · 2018–2019</span></h3>
        <ul class="mt-2 list-disc space-y-1.5 pl-5 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-stone-600 dark:text-stone-300">
          <li>Core engineer on the award-winning Connected Data Platform — production pipelines over NYC government records and third-party APIs on GCP (BigQuery, Airflow, GKE, Looker); entity resolution and a master metadata layer turning addresses, assessments and transactions into a real-estate knowledge graph.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h3 class="text-[17px] font-semibold text-stone-900 dark:text-stone-100">ABC Fitness Solutions <span class="font-normal text-stone-400 dark:text-stone-500">— Lead Data Architect · NYC · 2017–2018</span></h3>
        <ul class="mt-2 list-disc space-y-1.5 pl-5 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-stone-600 dark:text-stone-300">
          <li>Led an 8-person data team plus offshore contractors, reporting to the CTO, while hands-on in architecture and code; drove the monolith→microservices migration and built the cloud warehouse with PCI-compliant data standards (RDS, Redshift, Domo).</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h3 class="text-[17px] font-semibold text-stone-900 dark:text-stone-100">Consulting years <span class="font-normal text-stone-400 dark:text-stone-500">— Dell EMC, McKesson/RelayHealth, U.S. Bank/Elavon, Aloha Data · 2009–2017</span></h3>
        <ul class="mt-2 list-disc space-y-1.5 pl-5 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-stone-600 dark:text-stone-300">
          <li>Principal/Senior consultant delivering big-data and analytics platforms for PepsiCo, the Federal Reserve Bank of Philadelphia, the Australian Taxation Office, BC Hydro, the U.S. DoD, NYSE Euronext, Orbitz and Wellington Management; Greenplum/MPP implementations; HIPAA-compliant health data systems; $2B+ bank-acquisition migrations.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-10 grid gap-6 sm:grid-cols-2">
      <div>
        <h3 class="font-mono text-[11px] uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-stone-400 dark:text-stone-500">Education</h3>
        <ul class="mt-3 space-y-1.5 text-[14.5px] leading-relaxed text-stone-600 dark:text-stone-300">
          <li><strong class="text-stone-900 dark:text-stone-100">M.S. Artificial Intelligence</strong> — University of Texas at Austin (2027)</li>
          <li><strong class="text-stone-900 dark:text-stone-100">Post-graduate, AI &amp; ML</strong> — University of Texas at Austin (2023)</li>
          <li><strong class="text-stone-900 dark:text-stone-100">M.S. Software Engineering</strong> — Carnegie Mellon University (2008)</li>
          <li><strong class="text-stone-900 dark:text-stone-100">B.S. Computer Science</strong> — Franklin University (2006)</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h3 class="font-mono text-[11px] uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-stone-400 dark:text-stone-500">Toolkit</h3>
        <p class="mt-3 font-mono text-[12.5px] leading-relaxed text-stone-500 dark:text-stone-400">
          Python · SQL · dbt · Airflow · Dagster · Spark · Kafka · Flink · Iceberg · Trino · DuckDB
          · Snowflake · Databricks · BigQuery · PostgreSQL · Neo4j · PyTorch · MLflow · LangGraph
          · RAG · MCP · vLLM · pgvector · Great Expectations · OpenMetadata · Kubernetes · Terraform
          · Argo CD · AWS · GCP · Azure
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
    </div>
  </section>


</Layout>
